1199 0 obj
<<
/Title (1. Cluster labels are arbitrary in unsupervised learning Every time the algorithm runs, it groups the same images together correctly but assigns the group numbers \(1, 2, 3, 4, 5\) randomly. e.g: So "Forest" might be Cluster 1 in Run 1 and Cluster 4 in Run 2, shifting entire columns in the confusion matrix, even though nothing actually changed in the grouping.)
/Dest [30 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1185 0 R
/Next 1200 0 R
>>
endobj
1200 0 obj
<<
/Title (2. Eigen decomposition and  KMeans introduce randomness each run Spectral clustering computes eigenvectors internally  these can flip in sign or reorder slightly between runs due to mathematical non-uniqueness. KMeans then re-labels clusters from random starting points on top of that. This chain of randomness changes the column order every run, but since ACC/NMI/ARI use optimal label matching before scoring, the performance metrics stay identical.)
/Dest [30 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1185 0 R
/Prev 1199 0 R
>>
endobj
